schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Onboarding as trellis, not funnel
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    A reframe of member onboarding: a marketing "funnel" treats newcomers as
    throughput to be converted; a "trellis" is a pre-built structure (a known
    first-week path, a buddy, a graduation sequence) that's already in place
    before a newcomer arrives, so integration doesn't depend on the steward's
    personal, one-off effort each time.
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Framing device for the whole article: every subsequent recommendation
    (buddy system, first-week structure, role graduation) is presented as a
    plank of "the trellis."
  adjacent_meanings:
    - Marketing/sales funnel (the framing explicitly rejected as a model for community work)
    - ReFi DAO's Seed / Sapling / Canopy node-maturity model (a parallel growth metaphor cited in the same article)
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      "A funnel treats people as throughput. A community is a garden" — the
      article is explicit that the metaphor shift is meant to change steward
      behavior, not just language.
  tensions: []
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    None flagged — a general community-management framing device, not a claim
    about a specific person or tradition.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/onboarding-members.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
